# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code on this page was developed using the following requirements.\n"
"We recommend using these versions or newer.\n"
msgstr ""
"El código de esta página se desarrolló con los siguientes requisitos.\n"
"Recomendamos usar estas versiones o posteriores.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Use this page to upload a workflow, run it, and get its result. The example workflow optimizes and simulates a Qiskit circuit. It simulates the circuit on classical hardware, so it does not use QPU time.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Usa esta página para subir un workflow, ejecutarlo y obtener su resultado. El workflow de ejemplo optimiza y simula un circuito de Qiskit. Simula el circuito en hardware clásico, por lo que no consume tiempo de QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you begin, [install the client package and authenticate](/guides/install-managed-workflows).\n"
msgstr "Antes de empezar, [instala el paquete cliente y autentícate](/guides/install-managed-workflows).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Use AI skills (optional)\">\n"
"To deploy your own code with help from an AI assistant, use the AI skills in the [Qiskit Function templates repository](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-function-templates).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Usa habilidades de IA (opcional)\">\n"
"Para desplegar tu propio código con ayuda de un asistente de IA, usa las habilidades de IA del [repositorio de plantillas de Qiskit Function](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-function-templates).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write a workflow {#write-a-workflow}"
msgstr "Escribir un workflow {#write-a-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the folder structure {#create-the-folder-structure}"
msgstr "Crear la estructura de carpetas {#create-the-folder-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow is a folder of Python files with one entrypoint file. A managed workflow uploads everything in the folder, up to 50 MB, and runs the entrypoint as a script. Because a workflow uploads the whole folder, keep your local files, such as `deploy.ipynb`, outside the folder. Create the following layout:\n"
msgstr "Un managed workflow es una carpeta de archivos Python con un archivo de punto de entrada. Un managed workflow sube todo lo que hay en la carpeta, hasta 50 MB, y ejecuta el punto de entrada como un script. Como un workflow sube la carpeta completa, mantén tus archivos locales, como `deploy.ipynb`, fuera de la carpeta. Crea la siguiente estructura:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write the hello world entrypoint {#write-the-hello-world-entrypoint}"
msgstr "Escribir el punto de entrada hello world {#write-the-hello-world-entrypoint}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The entrypoint reads a circuit, optimizes and simulates it, and saves the counts and two-qubit depth. Save the following code as `source_files/hello_world.py`:\n"
msgstr "El punto de entrada lee un circuito, lo optimiza y lo simula, y guarda los conteos y la profundidad de dos qubits. Guarda el siguiente código como `source_files/hello_world.py`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"If you read this page as a notebook, the code cell for `hello_world.py` starts with the `%%writefile` [magic command](https://ipython.readthedocs.io/en/stable/interactive/magics.html#cellmagic-writefile). When you run this cell, it saves the code to the file instead of running the code.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Si lees esta página como un cuaderno, la celda de código de `hello_world.py` comienza con el [comando mágico](https://ipython.readthedocs.io/en/stable/interactive/magics.html#cellmagic-writefile) `%%writefile`. Cuando ejecutas esta celda, guarda el código en el archivo en lugar de ejecutarlo.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The entrypoint uses three functions from `qiskit_serverless`:\n"
msgstr "El punto de entrada usa tres funciones de `qiskit_serverless`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`get_arguments()` returns the keyword arguments that you pass to `run()`, as a dictionary. Each value must be JSON-serializable, or an object that the client can encode, such as a `QuantumCircuit`. Encoded objects arrive as the same objects that you passed.\n"
msgstr "`get_arguments()` devuelve como diccionario los argumentos con nombre que pasas a `run()`. Cada valor debe ser serializable en JSON, o un objeto que el cliente pueda codificar, como un `QuantumCircuit`. Los objetos codificados llegan como los mismos objetos que pasaste.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` sets the detailed status `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE`, which you can see while the job runs. See [Report progress with update_status()](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status).\n"
msgstr "`update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` establece el estado detallado `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE`, que puedes ver mientras el trabajo se ejecuta. Consulta [Informar del progreso con update_status()](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`save_result()` stores a JSON-serializable value that you read later with `job.result()`. The workflow returns the counts as a dictionary and the two-qubit depth of the optimized circuit as an integer.\n"
msgstr "`save_result()` almacena un valor serializable en JSON que lees más tarde con `job.result()`. El workflow devuelve los conteos como un diccionario y la profundidad de dos qubits del circuito optimizado como un entero.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output, such as the two-qubit depth, goes to the job's logs. To add timestamps and log levels, use the `logging` module. See [Write logs and handle errors](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors).\n"
msgstr "Todo lo que el workflow escribe en la salida estándar, como la profundidad de dos qubits, va a los registros del trabajo. Para añadir marcas de tiempo y niveles de registro, usa el módulo `logging`. Consulta [Escribir registros y gestionar errores](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the workflow {#upload-the-workflow}"
msgstr "Subir el workflow {#upload-the-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In your local notebook, run the following code from the `hello_world_project` folder. The code connects with your saved account, defines the workflow, and uploads it. `entrypoint` is the file that the workflow runs, and `working_dir` is the folder that you upload:\n"
msgstr "En tu cuaderno local, ejecuta el siguiente código desde la carpeta `hello_world_project`. El código se conecta con tu cuenta guardada, define el workflow y lo sube. `entrypoint` es el archivo que ejecuta el workflow, y `working_dir` es la carpeta que subes:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the workflow with inputs {#run-the-workflow-with-inputs}"
msgstr "Ejecutar el workflow con entradas {#run-the-workflow-with-inputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Construct a three-qubit GHZ circuit to pass to `hello_world` as an input:\n"
msgstr "Construye un circuito GHZ de tres qubits para pasarlo a `hello_world` como entrada:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run `hello_world` with the circuit and the number of shots as keyword arguments. The argument names match the keys that the entrypoint reads with `get_arguments()`:\n"
msgstr "Ejecuta `hello_world` con el circuito y el número de shots como argumentos con nombre. Los nombres de los argumentos coinciden con las claves que el punto de entrada lee con `get_arguments()`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`run()` returns a `Job` after the workflow queues the job. It does not wait for the job to run. The job continues in the cloud after you close your Python session. To find it again later, list your recent jobs with `client.jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "`run()` devuelve un `Job` después de que el workflow pone el trabajo en cola. No espera a que el trabajo se ejecute. El trabajo continúa en la nube después de que cierres tu sesión de Python. Para encontrarlo más tarde, lista tus trabajos recientes con `client.jobs()`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: add the web UI for job history when it is available. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get the status, result, and logs {#get-the-status-result-and-logs}"
msgstr "Obtener el estado, el resultado y los registros {#get-the-status-result-and-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Immediately after you call `run()`, the status is usually `QUEUED`:\n"
msgstr "Inmediatamente después de llamar a `run()`, el estado suele ser `QUEUED`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The status changes from `QUEUED` to `INITIALIZING`, `RUNNING`, and then `DONE`.\n"
msgstr "El estado cambia de `QUEUED` a `INITIALIZING`, `RUNNING` y luego `DONE`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.result()` waits until the job ends, then returns the value that the workflow passed to `save_result()`:\n"
msgstr "`job.result()` espera hasta que el trabajo termina y luego devuelve el valor que el workflow pasó a `save_result()`:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/managed-workflows/deploy-first-managed-workflow/extracted-outputs/b4e7a2fe-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/managed-workflows/deploy-first-managed-workflow/extracted-outputs/b4e7a2fe-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can read the logs while the job runs. The workflow uploads new lines about every 15 seconds. The logs include the line that the workflow printed:\n"
msgstr "Puedes leer los registros mientras el trabajo se ejecuta. El workflow sube líneas nuevas aproximadamente cada 15 segundos. Los registros incluyen la línea que imprimió el workflow:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Update the workflow {#update-the-workflow}"
msgstr "Actualizar el workflow {#update-the-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To change a workflow, edit its files and call `upload()` again with the same `title`. The new upload replaces the earlier one, and jobs that already started are not affected.\n"
msgstr "Para cambiar un workflow, edita sus archivos y llama de nuevo a `upload()` con el mismo `title`. La nueva subida reemplaza a la anterior, y los trabajos que ya comenzaron no se ven afectados.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fields such as `arguments_schema` and `sizes_map` keep their stored values when you omit them from the new upload.\n"
msgstr "Campos como `arguments_schema` y `sizes_map` conservan sus valores almacenados cuando los omites en la nueva subida.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Próximos pasos {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Define inputs and outputs](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs) to learn which argument and result types a workflow supports.\n"
"- [Declare dependencies](/guides/managed-workflow-dependencies) to use more Python packages in your workflow.\n"
"- [Run quantum jobs from a workflow](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows) to run your circuits on a QPU, report each stage, and track the QPU jobs.\n"
"- [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow) to learn all job statuses, debug a failed job, and find a job later.\n"
"- To start from working code, deploy one of the [Qiskit Function templates](/guides/qiskit-function-templates), or adapt a template for your own workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recomendaciones\">\n"
"- [Define entradas y salidas](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs) para saber qué tipos de argumentos y resultados admite un workflow.\n"
"- [Declara dependencias](/guides/managed-workflow-dependencies) para usar más paquetes de Python en tu workflow.\n"
"- [Ejecuta trabajos cuánticos desde un workflow](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows) para ejecutar tus circuitos en una QPU, informar de cada etapa y hacer seguimiento de los trabajos de QPU.\n"
"- [Ejecuta un managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow) para conocer todos los estados de los trabajos, depurar un trabajo fallido y encontrar un trabajo más tarde.\n"
"- Para partir de código que funciona, despliega una de las [plantillas de Qiskit Function](/guides/qiskit-function-templates), o adapta una plantilla para tu propio workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
